Q: Change position of plotly hover box R A: <p>Reusing some code from my answer <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/79521024/28479453">here</a> and <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/79503773/28479453">here</a>.</p>
<ul>
<li>Create your own <code>tooltip-div</code> style <code>custom-tooltip</code> using CSS. I took the CSS for the tooltip-triangle from <a href="https://css-tricks.com/the-little-triangle-in-the-tooltip/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">here</a>.</li>
<li>Whenever a point is hovered on, use the <a href="https://plotly.com/javascript/plotlyjs-events/#hover-event" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>plotly_onhover</code></a> event.</li>
<li>Within this event <code>e</code> there is information like which point was hovered on <code>e.points[0]</code> and the x-position of this point: <code>e.points[0].x</code>, y-position of this point: <code>e.points[0].y</code> but also <code>axis</code> details. We have to use <a href="https://community.plotly.com/t/how-to-customize-plotly-tooltip/332/16" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>yaxis.l2p</code></a>  from the y-axis in order to translate a y-position like <code>100</code> to the actual pixel-position <code>distX</code>. This is needed to place our <code>tooltip-div</code>!</li>
<li>To center the tooltip horizontally, we need to remove half of the tooltips' width, which is measured like <a href="https://johnkavanagh.co.uk/articles/element-dimensions-in-javascript-width-and-height/" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>tooltip?.clientWidth</code></a>: <code>tooltip.style.left = (distX - tooltip?.clientWidth / 2) + &quot;px&quot;;</code>.
Vertically we need to offset by <code>tooltip?.clientHeight - triangleHeight</code>.</li>
<li><code>tooltip.innerHTML = &quot;&lt;b&gt;Value: &quot; + pt.y + &quot;&lt;/b&gt;&quot;;</code> let's you define the content of the tooltip. Here you can basically use everything you want, tables, images, etc. I used the bold-tags to show how bolding text becomes easy now :).</li>
<li><code>tooltip.style.display = &quot;block&quot;;</code> actually shows the tooltip only when hovered, when unhovered, we hide it again using <code>tooltip.style.display = &quot;none&quot;</code>.</li>
</ul>
<pre><code>library(plotly)
library(htmlwidgets) # for adding custom JS in onRender(JS)

X &lt;- data.frame(x = 1:10, y = 1:10*10) 

js_code &lt;- paste0('
function(el, x) {
  var style = document.createElement(&quot;style&quot;);
  style.innerHTML = `
    :root {
      --triangle-base: 7px;   /* base width of the triangle below */
      --triangle-height: 7px; /* height of the triangle below */
      --triangle-top: 100%;   /* vertical alignment in percent of tooltip height. &lt; 100 % --&gt; hides behind tooltip */
      --triangle-left: 50%;   /* horizontal alignment in percent of tooltip width 50 % --&gt; centered */

      --triangle-color: grey;
    }
    .custom-tooltip {
      display: block;
      position: absolute;
      background-color: white;
      border: 1px solid #ddd;
      color: black;
      padding: 2px 6px;
      border-radius: 4px;
      z-index: 1000;
      box-shadow: 2px 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif; 
      &amp;::before {
        content: &quot;&quot;;
        position: absolute;
        top: var(--triangle-top);
        left: var(--triangle-left);

        border-width: var(--triangle-base);
        border-style: solid;
        border-color: transparent;
        border-top: var(--triangle-height) solid var(--triangle-color);

        transform: translateX(-50%);
      }
    }
  `;
  document.head.appendChild(style);

  var tooltip = document.createElement(&quot;div&quot;);
  tooltip.className = &quot;custom-tooltip&quot;;
  document.body.appendChild(tooltip);

  el.on(&quot;plotly_hover&quot;, function(e) {
    var pt = e.points[0];
    var yaxis = pt.yaxis;
    var xaxis = pt.xaxis;

    var distY = yaxis.l2p(pt.y) + yaxis._offset;
    var distX = xaxis.l2p(pt.x) + xaxis._offset;
    var triangleHeight = parseInt(
      getComputedStyle(document.documentElement).getPropertyValue(&quot;--triangle-height&quot;)
    );

    tooltip.innerHTML = &quot;&lt;b&gt;Value: &quot; + pt.y + &quot;&lt;/b&gt;&quot;;
    tooltip.style.display = &quot;block&quot;;
    tooltip.style.left = (distX - tooltip?.clientWidth / 2) + &quot;px&quot;;
    tooltip.style.top  = (distY - tooltip?.clientHeight - triangleHeight) + &quot;px&quot;;
  });

  el.on(&quot;plotly_unhover&quot;, function(e) {
    tooltip.style.display = &quot;none&quot;; 
  });

  }
')

plotly::plot_ly(data = X) |&gt;
  plotly::add_trace(
    x = ~x, 
    y = ~y, 
    type = 'bar', 
    hoverinfo = 'skip', 
    text = ~y
  ) |&gt;
  htmlwidgets::onRender(js_code)
</code></pre>
